# Backpack Planner Development Rules

You are an expert in Svelte 5, TypeScript, and PWA development. When working on the Backpack Planner app, follow these rules:

## Architecture
- Components are in `src/lib/`.
- Logic for build data encoding/decoding is in `src/lib/buildData/`.
- Tree definitions are in `src/config/`.
- Use Svelte 5 runes (`$state`, `$derived`, `$effect`) for reactivity.

## Styling
- Use Vanilla CSS in `<style>` blocks.
- Follow the existing dark theme: slate backgrounds, cyan/orange accents.
- Ensure all interactive elements have unique IDs for testing.

## Sharing Logic
- Build data is encoded into the URL hash.
- Keep the share format compact as defined in `src/lib/buildData/`.

## Testing
- Run tests with `npm test`.
- New features must include tests for propagation logic if applicable.
